function main()  #~ unexpected_character
    # Defect 242, 2026-10-04. Symptom: a file opening with a UTF-8 byte-order
    # mark, as PowerShell's `-Encoding utf8` writes one, was told twice: the
    # mark as `unexpected_character` at 1:1, then `unexpected_block` at this
    # first indented line, false, the mark having set the line above one
    # column deep. Cause: the lexer read the mark as a character of the first
    # line. It is told once now, at the mark, with the certain fix deleting
    # it, and the file is read from after it. This file opens with the mark
    # on purpose.
    print(1)
